#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175670 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/id #uuid "ef520918-4e4b-516b-acaa-57a14b5c1405" :question/math-academy-id "e-16134" :question/problem "Calculate $\\textrm{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n$x = \\big\\{6, \\: -2, \\: 7, \\: 1 \\big\\},\\qquad y = \\big\\{5, \\: -1, \\: 4, \\: 0 \\big\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets\n\n$$\nx=\\big\\{x_1,x_2, \\ldots, x_n \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny=\\big\\{y_1,y_2, \\ldots, y_n \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}(x,y) = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y})\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n y_i\n$$\n\nare the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot (6 + (-2) + 7 + 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 12 \\\\\n&= 3 \\\\\ny^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)y_{i} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot (5 + (-1) + 4 + 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 8 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nCov(x, y) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)(x_{i} - x^(―))(y_{i} - y^(―)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[(6 - 3)(5 - 2) + (-2 - 3)(-1 - 2) + (7 - 3)(4 - 2) + (1 - 3)(0 - 2)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[(3)(3) + (-5)(-3) + (4)(2) + (-2)(-2)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[9 + 15 + 8 + 4] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 36 \\\\\n&= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175671 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/id #uuid "33adfe2b-297e-5c52-8c4f-088d0c2b66e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-16136" :question/problem "A math teacher asked four of her students how many hours they had slept the night before an exam. The information she received is shown in the table above. Compute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overline{x}=5$ and $\\overline{y}=73$.\n\n| **Number of Hours of Sleep ($x$)** | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **Points Scored ($y$)** | $54$ | $68$ | $80$ | $90$ |" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets\n\n$$\nx=\\big\\{x_1,x_2, \\ldots, x_n \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny=\\big\\{y_1,y_2, \\ldots, y_n \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Cov}(x,y) = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y})\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n y_i\n$$\n\nare the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nCov(x, y) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)(x_{i} - x^(―))(y_{i} - y^(―)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[(2 - 5)(54 - 73) + (4 - 5)(68 - 73) + (6 - 5)(80 - 73) + (8 - 5)(90 - 73)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[(-3)(-19) + (-1)(-5) + (1)(7) + (3)(17)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[57 + 5 + 7 + 51] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 120 \\\\\n&= 30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9479bcac-f2e2-54e8-871a-0d853dfc3208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174193} {:answer/id #uuid "d761946c-ef86-5b2e-a53e-93beef450140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174194} {:answer/id #uuid "180fdc3d-4903-54c0-ab8f-7461c6609a86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174195} {:answer/id #uuid "3f64d110-e09b-5793-9342-f50897afc43f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174196} {:answer/id #uuid "52faad75-5450-5cb0-88f5-cf3a47cb425f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d761946c-ef86-5b2e-a53e-93beef450140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174194} :answer-field/id #uuid "3983408a-0e4a-5aa4-9444-ac9d3488dcb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174192}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b3a2205-203a-5056-a951-45e86cc0afea" :question/math-academy-id "q-134066" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nConsider the following data sets:\n$x = {4,-1, 0, 5}, y = {6, 3, 12, 11}$\nYou're given that $x^(―) = 2$ and $y^(―) = 8$. Calculate $Cov(x, y)$." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4-2)(6-8)+(-1-2)(3-8)+(0-2)(12-8)+(5-2)(11-8)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(2)(-2)+(-3)(-5)+(-2)(4)+(3)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[-4+15-8+9] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "886af3dd-5d8b-5ea6-bab2-129112bd4cc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174199} {:answer/id #uuid "8ede0f34-48ea-5d8e-a803-e12856c5dea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174200} {:answer/id #uuid "b6175ddc-549a-5d8c-8d2d-76cfbfa8af72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174201} {:answer/id #uuid "bef32139-a042-5774-8261-dadd61470199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174202} {:answer/id #uuid "00a79302-e254-5a84-80eb-2c282e9f701a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bef32139-a042-5774-8261-dadd61470199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174202} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a36726a-2900-52fa-ae79-efd63c28310c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174198}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23e49585-c742-508f-914d-dc9b039def78" :question/math-academy-id "q-134076" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nCalculate $Cov(x, y)$ for the following data sets:\n$x = {2, 3,-1, 4}, y = {4, 0, 2, 6}$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (2+3+(-1)+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (4+0+2+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(2-2)(4-3)+(3-2)(0-3)+(-1-2)(2-3)+(4-2)(6-3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(1)+(1)(-3)+(-3)(-1)+(2)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0-3+3+6] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "424e02af-f4a9-58f9-a554-57d66d3b337d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250168} {:answer/id #uuid "91eeff7f-d3a0-5d4d-ae3b-5fa399a23780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250169} {:answer/id #uuid "db2a4e14-07b6-52e6-95de-56695dbc4553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250170} {:answer/id #uuid "38fde69f-e301-5595-b0a3-1db051db0c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250171} {:answer/id #uuid "a2402940-7e7a-52bc-9b87-2070ba8256a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91eeff7f-d3a0-5d4d-ae3b-5fa399a23780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250169} :answer-field/id #uuid "19e6146b-0aae-570b-8af5-73b92e65d508" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250167}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72645700-d4a3-568b-b0a0-cd43ff9b3e63" :question/math-academy-id "q-134159" :question/problem "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={-1,\\,6,\\,2,\\,5},\\,y={-2,\\,5,\\,7,\\,6}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=3$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=4.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1-3)(-2-4)+(6-3)(5-4)+(2-3)(7-4)+(5-3)(6-4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-4)(-6)+(3)(1)+(-1)(3)+(2)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[24+3-3+4] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfa7bfde-094b-50c1-b6ac-d27e68fff615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250175} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6b1528-ebab-52f2-8ddb-7fbff700fd98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250176} {:answer/id #uuid "6de7a5dd-1335-5904-b3c5-e7953dee13fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250177} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc2ba8b-103f-5cad-afb8-47da8fa278b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250178} {:answer/id #uuid "477c9d89-1da4-57fb-bf73-bcfd2fee3e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbc2ba8b-103f-5cad-afb8-47da8fa278b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250178} :answer-field/id #uuid "b91758e8-0361-56ed-bae0-7a111f2d7c0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250174}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e09a6146-6ce2-509b-a961-b8096bb274f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-134163" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={-2,\\,5,\\,1,\\,4},\\,y={-4,\\,2,\\,4,\\,-6}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ((-2)+5+1+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ((-4)+2+4+(-6)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2\\,-\\,2)(-4\\,-\\,(-1))+(5\\,-\\,2)(2\\,-\\,(-1))+(1\\,-\\,2)(4\\,-\\,(-1))+(4\\,-\\,2)(-6\\,-\\,(-1))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-4)(-3)+(3)(3)+(-1)(5)+(2)(-5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[12+9-5-10] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dac05f62-31e5-5c6a-8e2e-e750b0495b18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250182} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad8e44c-1870-5794-b5f8-043c3e22b43e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250183} {:answer/id #uuid "2b7f79c5-732d-5349-91c4-73af9ef2e11d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250184} {:answer/id #uuid "ba0a489e-d697-57a1-98c4-7ee0a7430f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250185} {:answer/id #uuid "9f483b35-8d70-5cd5-9433-ebfeea67b2eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba0a489e-d697-57a1-98c4-7ee0a7430f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250185} :answer-field/id #uuid "d966d4f0-7ef8-51a6-9516-2d05552856e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250181}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7fed5d4-3bcd-519f-bdfd-0ef5f602eac6" :question/math-academy-id "q-134204" :question/problem "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $15$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Weight, in kg ($y$)** | $30$ | $34$ | $38$ | $42$ |\n\nTara plays soccer. The table above shows the ages and corresponding weights of four of Tara's teammates.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=12$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=36.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(10\\,-\\,12)(30\\,-\\,36)+(11\\,-\\,12)(34\\,-\\,36)+(12\\,-\\,12)(38\\,-\\,36)+(15\\,-\\,12)(42\\,-\\,36)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2)(-6)+(-1)(-2)+(0)(2)+(3)(6)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[12+2+0+18] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09bd2b12-deaf-5806-a3b1-df6616adc0f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250189} {:answer/id #uuid "787f69af-f26b-502d-97d0-9d6198e11534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250190} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b4f8fb-494d-5a70-8728-8689c901d3e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250191} {:answer/id #uuid "08160a91-c4c9-5fdf-b718-3bbf6edb47f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250192} {:answer/id #uuid "2c631e10-f31e-5a1a-b9c3-f337fcc63909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08160a91-c4c9-5fdf-b718-3bbf6edb47f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250192} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfb98824-e5f0-5246-887d-01a4dacb0afa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250188}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22f79cc9-53e8-5975-ba0e-1f7352fee98e" :question/math-academy-id "q-134212" :question/problem "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $45$ | $39$ | $43$ | $37$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **IQ Score ($y$)** | $90$ | $82$ | $75$ | $85$ |\n\nThe table above shows the ages and corresponding IQ scores of some of Jerry's colleagues. Compute the covariance of the data sets." :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (45+39+43+37) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 164 \\\\  & =41 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (90+82+75+85) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 332 \\\\  & =83\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(45\\,-\\,41)(90\\,-\\,83)\\,+\\,(39\\,-\\,41)(82\\,-\\,83)\\,+\\,(43\\,-\\,41)(75\\,-\\,83)\\,+\\,(37\\,-\\,41)(85\\,-\\,83)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4)(7)+(-2)(-1)+(2)(-8)+(-4)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[28+2-16-8] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dff56c0-c25c-52c8-8666-694965934db2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250196} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c38b12-42bb-596c-8729-47932419343d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250197} {:answer/id #uuid "fa2008e0-ae40-5538-82cb-9ace9229783c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250198} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a8a514-672f-5215-8c5f-2159396fbed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250199} {:answer/id #uuid "d730056a-622f-53a9-922b-b5b1a8066fe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d730056a-622f-53a9-922b-b5b1a8066fe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250200} :answer-field/id #uuid "610bd9ea-e98d-5e59-9fb2-ad97b22dd6fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250195}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "884ebce5-07f2-5ea2-8fcf-3e6457f8e084" :question/math-academy-id "q-134216" :question/problem "| **Temperature, in ${}^{∘}C$ ($x$)** | $24$ | $26$ | $24$ | $22$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Lemonade Sales, in $$$ ($y$)** | $180$ | $202$ | $190$ | $140$ |\n\nThe owner of a lemonade stand keeps track of how much they sell in relation to the daily temperature. The table above shows the data they collected over the past four days. Compute the covariance of the data sets." :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (24+26+24+22) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 96 \\\\  & =24 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (180+202+190+140) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 712 \\\\  & =178\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(24\\,-\\,24)(180\\,-\\,178)\\,+\\,(26\\,-\\,24)(202\\,-\\,178)\\,+\\,(24\\,-\\,24)(190\\,-\\,178)\\,+\\,(22\\,-\\,24)(140\\,-\\,178)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(2)+(2)(24)+(0)(12)+(-2)(-38)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+48+0+76] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 124 \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a60f2c3-a13e-540b-81f9-62416a547ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250203} {:answer/id #uuid "22a64d10-3037-500b-a021-9eb735739265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250204} {:answer/id #uuid "631e4cfe-5429-5d2b-93c7-e9f26cb3e886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250205} {:answer/id #uuid "c22f7813-7090-542f-bf2b-8e903639b7bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250206} {:answer/id #uuid "3efcc81a-e897-5c34-adbd-1ed5a09e60dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22a64d10-3037-500b-a021-9eb735739265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250204} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e898313-b3f4-53e2-a1dc-c3847bd672f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250202}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2360b2d2-9647-5235-8ecd-7a1e7a025609" :question/math-academy-id "q-134221" :question/problem "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Shoe Size (USA) ($y$)** | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $8$ |\n\nMr. Damon recorded the age and shoe size of four tennis players at his academy. The table above shows the information he collected. Compute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=10$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=8.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(7-10)(7-8)+(9-10)(8-8)+(11-10)(9-8)+(13-10)(8-8)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-3)(-1)+(-1)(0)+(1)(1)+(3)(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[3+0+1+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb5da30f-0d71-5526-9049-aed729fc3af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250210} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6708de-2226-517a-8252-d1db267f48ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250211} {:answer/id #uuid "8d792c5e-c88c-5a0c-9662-2d3e92cf1e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250212} {:answer/id #uuid "6c64d1b4-c6cf-5924-880c-3e681467fc2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250213} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf15134-bad2-5cbd-96b4-b60133522f52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb5da30f-0d71-5526-9049-aed729fc3af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250210} :answer-field/id #uuid "fde9dfcc-7842-526a-bcb1-4d3fdca6bd9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250209}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a8b19b6-473c-5ece-b5c9-29853f4e074a" :question/math-academy-id "q-149561" :question/problem "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $12$ | $12$ | $14$ | $14$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Weight, in lbs ($y$)** | $85$ | $90$ | $97$ | $100$ |\n\nMike plays baseball. The table above shows the ages and corresponding weights of four of Mike's teammates.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets." :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (12+12+14+14) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 52 \\\\  & =13 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (85+90+97+100) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 372 \\\\  & =93\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(12\\,-\\,13)(85\\,-\\,93)+(12\\,-\\,13)(90\\,-\\,93)+(14\\,-\\,13)(97\\,-\\,93)+(14\\,-\\,13)(100\\,-\\,93)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-8)+(-1)(-3)+(1)(4)+(1)(7)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8+3+4+7] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =5.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Covariance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da48ce4c-1657-589a-b46f-8b5e3b40f45e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250217} {:answer/id #uuid "17828aec-298b-546c-b1fb-3897146ccb81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250218} {:answer/id #uuid "3d64b483-8edb-5149-8842-f24a15d405a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250219} {:answer/id #uuid "05844aaa-f0ea-5ba0-87fe-d8ddf446f955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250220} {:answer/id #uuid "3a799b82-a49b-5f08-930a-4abd607cbc93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a799b82-a49b-5f08-930a-4abd607cbc93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250221} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cee887f-e052-5506-af32-e9f4bfbefa71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250216}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ea5cea6-ac74-57bd-b531-a5313a9a9126" :question/math-academy-id "q-149616" :question/problem "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={12,\\,7,\\,6,\\,3},\\,y={-4,\\,-6,\\,-4,\\,-2}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=7$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=-4.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(12-7)(-4-(-4))+(7-7)(-6-(-4)) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(6-7)(-4-(-4))+(3-7)(-2-(-4))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(5)(0)+(0)(-2)+(-1)(0)+(-4)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+0+0-8] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
